WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.913 --> 00:00:06.996
- The Shop...

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:13.966
- I've been doing hair over 50 years.

00:00:13.966 --> 00:00:18.337
Been a barber since 1989,
something like that.

00:00:18.337 --> 00:00:21.170
It's the only shop I ever been in.

00:00:23.624 --> 00:00:26.409
- I couldn't think of no better person.

00:00:26.409 --> 00:00:28.289
I came up, when you go to a barber shop,

00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:30.135
you go for not only a haircut,

00:00:30.135 --> 00:00:33.361
knowledge, wisdom,
respect, all those things.

00:00:33.361 --> 00:00:36.961
We're not only barbers,
we're here to educate people

00:00:36.961 --> 00:00:40.238
who needs it, to advise students,

00:00:40.238 --> 00:00:41.926
try to be the best they could be.

00:00:41.926 --> 00:00:45.805
A positive image, that's
what it's all about.

00:00:45.805 --> 00:00:46.638
- I didn't start gettin'
haircuts 'til like

00:00:46.638 --> 00:00:48.380
my senior year of high school.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:49.596
Me and my friends would basically

00:00:49.596 --> 00:00:51.088
schedule 'em at the same time,

00:00:51.088 --> 00:00:53.093
and it was kinda like
a little social event,

00:00:53.093 --> 00:00:57.531
a place to talk sports,
talk girls, talk everything.

00:00:57.531 --> 00:01:00.196
I have cheated on my
barber, I cheated on him

00:01:00.196 --> 00:01:02.664
at a shop that was
nearby, and it was like,

00:01:02.664 --> 00:01:05.797
legit insecurity, like worried
I was going to run into him,

00:01:05.797 --> 00:01:07.515
so I went, and the other dude cut my hair,

00:01:07.515 --> 00:01:08.833
but it felt dirty.

00:01:08.833 --> 00:01:10.358
There's a great significance,

00:01:10.358 --> 00:01:11.638
the barber shop in black culture.

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:12.760
Sometimes it's a good place

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.110
to come get your opinions out.

00:01:15.110 --> 00:01:17.628
So you gotta have jokes,
or you gotta be prepared

00:01:17.628 --> 00:01:19.591
to get roasted, and it's kind of intense.

00:01:19.591 --> 00:01:20.811
I feel like it just is a culture,

00:01:20.811 --> 00:01:23.439
but it, I mean it might vary a little bit

00:01:23.439 --> 00:01:25.757
from shop to shop, but for the most part,

00:01:25.757 --> 00:01:27.947
you can expect to be
entertained somewhat socially

00:01:27.947 --> 00:01:31.034
as much as you're going
to get your hair cut.

00:01:31.034 --> 00:01:33.873
- I remember when I got the
whole idea to become a barber.

00:01:33.873 --> 00:01:36.798
I was in temporary, and there
was a dude named Norman,

00:01:36.798 --> 00:01:39.224
at our school that cut hair,
he didn't play basketball,

00:01:39.224 --> 00:01:41.024
he didn't play football,
nothin' like that.

00:01:41.024 --> 00:01:43.065
He was the barber, and that's
what everybody knew him for.

00:01:43.065 --> 00:01:45.344
He's the first person I looked
up to, in a different world.

00:01:45.344 --> 00:01:47.142
I told him one day, that, like 'bruh,

00:01:47.142 --> 00:01:49.088
you're the one who
inspired me to be a barber.

00:01:49.088 --> 00:01:50.823
I don't know where I would
be at in life right now,

00:01:50.823 --> 00:01:52.031
if it wasn't for me cutting hair,

00:01:52.031 --> 00:01:54.470
so it's like, I kinda
owe all of this to him.

00:01:54.470 --> 00:01:55.563
- That's love right there, man.

00:01:55.563 --> 00:01:57.244
That energy exchange is very important.

00:01:57.244 --> 00:02:00.051
- When I grew up the barber
shop is where little boys went

00:02:00.051 --> 00:02:02.008
to basically kinda learn how to be men,

00:02:02.008 --> 00:02:03.290
you kinda grow up in a barber shop,

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.329
I mean, you learn a lot just
from sittin' and listening.

00:02:05.329 --> 00:02:08.440
We couldn't go to say, white barber shops.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:11.105
We needed that place to feel safe.

00:02:11.105 --> 00:02:13.121
The barber shop is where
men can go to be men,

00:02:13.121 --> 00:02:14.702
away from, you know I'm sayin', the women,

00:02:14.702 --> 00:02:15.540
and we can talk about the things

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:16.604
that we really want to talk about.

00:02:16.604 --> 00:02:20.836
Whether it's women, sports, sex, cars,

00:02:20.836 --> 00:02:21.794
you know what I mean?

00:02:21.794 --> 00:02:24.106
You kinda get to be who you
really are in a barber shop

00:02:24.106 --> 00:02:25.851
'cause no one's here to judge.

00:02:25.851 --> 00:02:27.321
That's what makes a barber shop fun.

00:02:27.321 --> 00:02:28.154
You don't wanna go anywhere where

00:02:28.154 --> 00:02:30.055
you can't have fun and
you can't be yourself.

00:02:30.055 --> 00:02:32.673
- The energy, the energy that's goin' on

00:02:32.673 --> 00:02:35.345
inside the shop, it's very intense.

00:02:35.345 --> 00:02:37.759
At times, it's a little intimidating,

00:02:37.759 --> 00:02:39.127
you know, when you walk in, especially,

00:02:39.127 --> 00:02:40.862
if you looking a little goofy, but,

00:02:40.862 --> 00:02:43.522
once the cut was done I knew I was fresh.

00:02:43.522 --> 00:02:45.479
- That's another reason
I love being a barber,

00:02:45.479 --> 00:02:47.838
is like, being able to
give cats that confidence,

00:02:47.838 --> 00:02:48.671
you know what I mean?

00:02:48.671 --> 00:02:50.312
After you get a fresh cut,
you know the confidence

00:02:50.312 --> 00:02:52.068
that somebody walk outta
the barber shop with,

00:02:52.068 --> 00:02:53.418
being able to give people that?

00:02:53.418 --> 00:02:54.552
Like, I love that, man.

00:02:54.552 --> 00:02:56.181
- That's why a lotta cats
come to the barber shop,

00:02:56.181 --> 00:02:57.306
don't even need haircuts, they'll just

00:02:57.306 --> 00:02:58.537
come there for that environment.

00:02:58.537 --> 00:03:00.344
A barber shop is a place to really kinda

00:03:00.344 --> 00:03:03.031
hone in on that, because
we are a community,

00:03:03.031 --> 00:03:05.840
and that's kinda what we're here for.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:08.628
- People like to see their pictures.

00:03:08.628 --> 00:03:11.092
I started out takin'
pictures, so well kids,

00:03:11.092 --> 00:03:12.422
so they'd give it to their parents,

00:03:12.422 --> 00:03:13.755
'cause when I was comin' up,

00:03:13.755 --> 00:03:15.040
I guess we couldn't afford cameras

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:17.635
and this and that, so I started doing it

00:03:17.635 --> 00:03:21.552
to pass 'em out to the kids, or whoever

00:03:22.584 --> 00:03:24.809
don't have no picture of
themself when they were young.

00:03:24.809 --> 00:03:28.192
You know, pictures hold memories,

00:03:28.192 --> 00:03:31.507
and I like to look at 'em sometimes,

00:03:31.507 --> 00:03:33.423
and think what I was doing at that time.

00:03:33.423 --> 00:03:37.419
- This is actually the
first barber shop I remember

00:03:37.419 --> 00:03:40.795
being in, like everybody
definitely has a barber shop,

00:03:40.795 --> 00:03:42.758
but the way that we do,

00:03:42.758 --> 00:03:44.659
the barber shop is completely different.

00:03:44.659 --> 00:03:47.935
As I look around, just,
it's so much that is

00:03:47.935 --> 00:03:52.131
very unique to this
space, this black space.

00:03:52.131 --> 00:03:56.776
Everything that the barber
is, they put on these walls,

00:03:56.776 --> 00:04:00.192
and it helps attach
themselves to their heritage,

00:04:00.192 --> 00:04:03.816
but it also attaches
themselves to their practice.

00:04:03.816 --> 00:04:07.349
I think yep, this is a museum,

00:04:07.349 --> 00:04:09.849
a gallery space within itself.

00:04:10.924 --> 00:04:13.643
- 'Cause it does,
specially the older guys,

00:04:13.643 --> 00:04:17.711
we need to be more toward our youngsters.

00:04:17.711 --> 00:04:21.564
I love people, if I could help anyone.

00:04:21.564 --> 00:04:24.279
A boy, got race, creed or color, you know,

00:04:24.279 --> 00:04:27.029
that's what it's all about to me.

00:04:28.359 --> 00:04:32.192
It's not only our people,
it's for all people.

00:04:41.585 --> 00:04:45.752
I did women hair up until 67,
I shoulda' stayed with women.

00:04:47.961 --> 00:04:50.826
I'd probably be a little
bit more wealthier now.

